WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
In the Yuan dynasty's final years the court was corrupt and officials were greedy, and the common people's lives grew harder and harder.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:17.318
Disasters came without end and taxes were heavy; social conflicts grew worse by the day, and the people truly could not go on living this way.

00:00:17.668 --> 00:00:27.148
Around the year 1351, common people wearing red headscarves rose up one after another to resist Yuan rule.

00:00:27.498 --> 00:00:32.658
The Red Turban ranks kept growing, and the uprising spread rapidly to every region.

00:00:33.008 --> 00:00:37.352
At dusk, the column carried torches as it marched toward the distance.

00:00:37.702 --> 00:00:45.262
The Yuan armies retreated defeat after defeat; the court's control grew weaker and weaker, and every region fell into chaos.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:52.626
The uprising gravely weakened the Yuan dynasty, and created the conditions for new political forces to rise.

00:00:52.976 --> 00:00:58.016
At sunrise, the people gazed into the distance, their hearts full of hope.

